From a5859b382b45180a452613e7871241cb4f8c7756 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:03:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: behaviour tests of the cuda-clang and
 hip-clang configurations

- The behaviours are now tested with the cuda-clang and hip-clang
  (NVIDIA platform) configurations, which were only tested with
  material properties.
- clang only supports the versions of CUDA released before it. The
  TFEL_CLANG_CUDA_PATH variable of cmake selects the CUDA toolkit used by
  clang (by default, the one of nvcc). It defines the TFEL_CLANG_CUDA_PATH
  and TFEL_CLANG_CUDA_LIBRARY_DIR substitutions.
- The include directory of HIP is given to clang with -I, not -isystem.
  When HIP is installed in /usr, -isystem /usr/include places it before
  the headers of the C++ standard library and breaks their #include_next
  directives. Compilers ignore -I for a standard system directory.
- The configuration files use -O2, as the other configurations.
---
